2. The Non-Negotiable Governance Principle

VRYOH detects and interprets only — it never prescribes operational actions. No recommendations, no action items, no "you should" language, ever, anywhere in the product (dashboard, reports, or drafts). Every response draft requires human approval before it reaches the public. This is a permanent architectural and brand commitment, not a feature toggle — it's central to the trust proposition and should not be softened in any commercial or marketing framing.

3. Product Architecture (business-relevant summary — not for engineering depth)

Three core pillars: DETECT / GOVERN / DELIVER.

The product is built as a chain of automated stages that take a raw guest review and turn it into: (a) a governed, brand-voice-matched draft response awaiting human sign-off, and (b) structured intelligence delivered to the operator on a schedule.

Three managed outputs:

Individual governed response drafts, calibrated to the emotional signal and risk level of each review, with elevated handling for dignity-risk situations (e.g., discrimination allegations).
Weekly Review Intelligence Brief (Monday mornings) — top pain points, emotional signal distribution, week-over-week trend, top signals needing attention.
Monthly Review Pattern Report (1st of month) — 30-day pattern summary, trend lines, dignity-risk events flagged.

Delivery SLAs: 48-hour turnaround on response drafts; weekly brief on Monday; monthly report on the 1st.

Bilingual (English/Spanish): Confirmed live and working in production as of a July 15, 2026 test — not aspirational. The Spanish drafting pipeline was built as a fully independent, natively-authored chain (not a translation layer bolted onto English), which is a genuine differentiator and a better craft story than most competitors would have.

